%
O1099 (STOCK CHECK - POSITIONING ONLY, NOTHING IS CUT)
(RUN THIS IN THE SIMULATOR TO FIND OUT WHERE THE BLANK ACTUALLY IS)
(EVERY MOVE IS A RAPID TO A KNOWN COORDINATE FOLLOWED BY M00)
(AT EACH STOP, LOOK AT THE TOOL NOSE AGAINST THE STOCK AND WRITE)
(DOWN THE FIRST STOP WHERE THE NOSE IS CLEAR OF THE MATERIAL)
()
(PART 1 FINDS HOW FAR THE RAW FACE STANDS PROUD OF Z0)
(PART 2 FINDS THE RAW OUTSIDE DIAMETER)
()
(THE TOOL NEVER FEEDS - IF IT LOOKS LIKE IT IS INSIDE THE STOCK,)
(THAT IS THE ANSWER, NOT A CRASH)
()

G21 G18 G40 G80 G99
G28 U0. W0.
T0101
G97 S300 M03

(=== PART 1  WHERE IS THE RAW FACE IN Z ===)
(NOSE PARKED ON THE OD LINE, STEPPING AWAY FROM THE CHUCK)
(THE FIRST STOP WHERE THE NOSE SITS CLEAR OF THE FACE = THE PROTRUSION)
G00 X50. Z20.
X36.
Z0.
M00 (STOP 1 -- Z0.0)
Z1.
M00 (STOP 2 -- Z1.0)
Z2.
M00 (STOP 3 -- Z2.0)
Z3.
M00 (STOP 4 -- Z3.0)
Z4.
M00 (STOP 5 -- Z4.0)
Z6.
M00 (STOP 6 -- Z6.0)
Z8.
M00 (STOP 7 -- Z8.0)
Z12.
M00 (STOP 8 -- Z12.0  IF THE FACE IS STILL LEFT OF HERE, IT IS BAR STOCK)

(=== PART 2  WHAT IS THE RAW OUTSIDE DIAMETER ===)
(NOSE PARKED WELL CLEAR IN Z, CLOSING IN ON THE OD)
(THE LAST STOP WHERE THE NOSE IS STILL CLEAR = THE RAW OD)
G00 X60. Z-4.
M00 (STOP 9  -- D60.0)
X50.
M00 (STOP 10 -- D50.0)
X45.
M00 (STOP 11 -- D45.0)
X42.
M00 (STOP 12 -- D42.0)
X40.
M00 (STOP 13 -- D40.0)
X38.
M00 (STOP 14 -- D38.0  <- THE BLANK THE PROGRAMS ASSUME)
X36.
M00 (STOP 15 -- D36.0)

G00 X60. Z20.
G28 U0. W0.
M05
M30
%
